    {
      "role": "hint",
      "content": "\u003cdiv class\u003d\"step_content\"\u003e\n \u003cp\u003ePress \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_19850\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/qenter.gif\" onmouseout\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOut()\" onmouseover\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOver(\u0026quot;token_19850\u0026quot;,144)\"\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e",
      "figure": null,
      "figures": null
    },
    {
      "role": "step",
      "content": "\u003cdiv class\u003d\"step_content\"\u003e\n \u003cp\u003ePress \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_19851\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/qenter.gif\" onmouseout\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOut()\" onmouseover\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOver(\u0026quot;token_19851\u0026quot;,144)\"\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003eThe calculator gives the list of values:\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003e0, 1, 0.5, 0.66667, 0.6, 0.625, 0.61538, 0.61905, 0.61765,\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003e0.61818, 0.61798, 0.61806, 0.61803, 0.61804, 0.61803\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\u003cimg class\u003d\"graphimgstatic id\u003d\" figure-3 src\u003d\"/modules/gcprealgpractice/gcprealgpractice_8_1_realnumbersandthepythagoreantheorem_9d_70/f-70-9d-2.gif\"\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e",
      "figure": null,
      "figures": null
    },
    {
      "role": "hint",
      "content": "\u003cdiv class\u003d\"step_content\"\u003e\n \u003cp\u003eComment on the behavior of this sequence.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e",
      "figure": null,
      "figures": null
    },
    {
      "role": "step",
      "content": "\u003cdiv class\u003d\"step_content\"\u003e\n \u003cp\u003eThe values get closer and closer to a value somewhere between 0.61803 and 0.61804.\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003e(The real value is\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003e0.61803398874989484820458683436564..., and is known as the \u003ci\u003egolden mean\u003c/i\u003e. This number occurs frequently in biology.)\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003eNote also that the sequence is alternately increasing and decreasing; first it increases from 0 to 1, then decreases from 1 to 0.5, then increases to \u003cimg width\u003d\"21\" height\u003d\"41\" src\u003d\"/modules/gcprealgpractice/gcprealgpractice_8_1_realnumbersandthepythagoreantheorem_9d_70/image038.gif\" class\u003d\"middle\"\u003e etc.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e",
      "figure": null,
